 class="enc-snip">Urus Khan was a Jochid ruler of the White Horde, in the eastern part of the Golden Horde, from about 1368 until his death in 1377.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/urzana"><span class="enc-name">Urzana</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Urzana was king of Musasir, a small mountain state between Assyria and Urartu famous for the temple of the god Haldi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/us-oil-embargo-against-japan"><span class="enc-name">US oil embargo against Japan</span><span class="enc-type">Crisis · 1941</span><span class="enc-snip">The US oil embargo against Japan was the cutting off of American oil exports to Japan in 1941, imposed in response to Japanese expansion in Indochina.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/usain-bolt"><span class="enc-name">Usain Bolt</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Usain Bolt is a Jamaican sprinter widely regarded as the greatest of all time.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/usama-ibn-munqidh"><span class="enc-name">Usama ibn Munqidh</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Usama ibn Munqidh was an Arab poet, soldier and courtier of the Munqidhite family of Shaizar in northern Syria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/usambara-mountains"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/usambara-mountains.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Usambara Mountains</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Usambara Mountains are a range in north-eastern Tanzania, part of the ancient Eastern Arc Mountains.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/usatges-of-barcelona"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/usatges-of-barcelona.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Usatges of Bar